From 3d5a32d000212d70922f33678ef263c0da347b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gennady Uraltsev <gennady.uraltsev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:40:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Enter in aligned nesting the table instead of adding a
 row

math-edit.scm has an old kbd-enter for aligned that treats its content as one
formula: it splits it at the first relation into two columns and wraps it in a
new table.  aligned now normally already contains a table (created with make,
imported from LaTeX, or built by the gathered/aligned tools), so each Enter
wrapped the whole table into the first cell of a new table, producing a
staircase of nested tables.

Which handler won depended on module load order against the generic
table-markup-context handler in table-edit.scm.  Only use the legacy handler
when the aligned block is not already a table, so the table handler always adds
a row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 TeXmacs/progs/math/math-edit.scm | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TeXmacs/progs/math/math-edit.scm b/TeXmacs/progs/math/math-edit.scm
index c3e7597f0..45e432db0 100644
--- a/TeXmacs/progs/math/math-edit.scm
+++ b/TeXmacs/progs/math/math-edit.scm
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 ) ;tm-define
 
 (tm-define (kbd-enter t shift?)
-  (:require (tree-is? t 'aligned))
+  (:require (and (tree-is? t 'aligned) (not (table-markup-context? t))))
   (let* ((c (tree-ref t 0))
          (l0 (concat-decompose c))
          (l2 (list-scatter l0 binary-relation? #t))

